  "description": "A dual-panel interactive tool where students copy a given angle from a source location to a target location using ruler and compass. The left panel shows the original angle with its arc and chord. The right panel is the workspace where students replicate the construction step by step. The tool highlights how SSS congruence guarantees the copied angle is exact, and shows the chord transfer as the critical measurement step. Built with Singularity design system (Poppins font, #4A4DC9 primary, #FF7212 accent, #533086 purple). Responsive layout stacks panels vertically below 640px. Component exported as both named and default export for universal bundler compatibility.",
  "objective_id": "M2.S10.T10.O1",
  "teaching_notes": "The chord BC is the critical measurement — it encodes the angle size within the fixed-radius arc. Emphasise that we never measure the angle in degrees; instead, we transfer the triangle that defines it. This connects to repeating patterns where exact angle copies are needed for each unit.",
  "implementation_notes": {
    "export_strategy": "Main component declared as plain 'function AngleCopyingTool()' with separate 'export { AngleCopyingTool }' (named) and 'export default AngleCopyingTool' (default) at end of file, replacing the original inline 'export default function' declaration."
  },
